# {{SYSTEM_NAME}} Screen-Creation Agents — Claude Code Handoff

Orchestration layer for the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} **screen-creation** role agents. This context revolves around
**building consumer screens + coded prototypes** by *consuming* the published {{SYSTEM_NAME}} library. The
**design system itself lives in a separate context** (`{{DS_REPO}}`). Complements — does not
replace — `CONTEXT.md` / `CLAUDE.md` (project facts + working preferences) and `DESIGN.md` (design
principles + benchmarks, shared with the DS context).

---

## Install

`.claude/` (the `ux-designer` + `ui-designer` agents and the `/design-review`, `/consumer-audit`
commands) and `DESIGN.md` are **committed to this repo** — a fresh clone already has the roster, no
copy step. (`/agents` opens an interactive panel inside a terminal Claude Code session to verify.)

The design-system roster (`ds-steward`, `component-designer`, `brand-designer`, `/design-system-check`,
`/binding-audit`, `/drift-check`) is **not here** — it lives in `{{DS_REPO}}`.

---

## The organizing principle — define before you build, compose don't reinvent

Two **core** roles drive the pipeline, plus two **supporting** roles (an independent reviewer and a
migrator), each owning a distinct **write-surface** and **moment in the pipeline**, so they never collide.

| Role | Write surface | Owns (object type) |
|---|---|---|
| `ux-designer` | SPECS only (markdown/docs, FigJam-level flow diagrams) | flows · IA · journeys · state matrices · interaction + a11y behavior specs · acceptance criteria · functional microcopy |
| `ui-designer` | CONSUMER Figma file `{{CONSUMER_FIGMA_KEY}}` (screen frames, layout, composition, states) | pixel-perfect, system-compliant screens composed from {{SYSTEM_NAME}} · build-time design-review self-check · consumer drift sweeps |
| `flow-reviewer` | read-only (review output) | INDEPENDENT heuristic evaluation of screens + flows — runs the `ux-flow-review` canon; the expert-review gate |
| `data-analyst` | read-only (analysis output) | EMPIRICAL validation — turns prototype analytics into benchmarked evidence (the `usability-analytics` canon); feeds `ux-designer` |
| `consumer-migrator` | CONSUMER file(s) (instance swaps + override re-application) | propagating a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish across consumers — runs the `rebind` procedure; confirms changes are consumed |

**Mental model:** `ux-designer` defines the right thing (what + why) → `ui-designer` builds it right
(compose {{SYSTEM_NAME}}, pixel fidelity + system compliance) → the screens are **usability-validated via a
coded prototype** → the **validated** screens hand off to product + engineering / go live. A {{SYSTEM_NAME}}
gap found mid-build routes to the **DS context** (`ds-steward` / `component-designer`) → they
tokenize/build/publish → this context consumes the published result.

