## Roster

| Agent | Owns | Fires on |
|---|---|---|
| `ux-designer` | flows, IA, state matrices, interaction/a11y specs, research synthesis, acceptance criteria, functional microcopy | "plan the UX for X", "map the flow", "what states does this need", "write the spec", "synthesize this research", "what should this error/empty state say" |
| `ui-designer` | composing {{SYSTEM_NAME}} into pixel-perfect consumer screens, build-time design-review self-check, consumer-file drift sweep | "build/recreate the X screen", "compose this flow in Figma", "sweep the consumer file for drift" |
| `flow-reviewer` | INDEPENDENT heuristic evaluation of screens + flows (the `ux-flow-review` canon) | "review this screen/flow", "heuristic evaluation", "is this usable / AA-compliant", "evaluate this journey" |
| `data-analyst` | turning prototype analytics into screen-validation evidence (the `usability-analytics` canon) | "analyze the usability data", "what does the data say", "benchmark SEQ / task success / time-on-task", "where are users dropping off" |
| `consumer-migrator` | propagating a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish across consumer files (the `rebind` procedure) | "migrate the consumer onto the new X", "the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} update shipped — sweep the consumer", "confirm the publish is consumed" |

**Shared building blocks** — reusable pieces every relevant role loads, so behavior never drifts:
- **`ux-flow-review` skill** = the single heuristic-evaluation canon (5 frameworks + {{DOMAIN}} + WCAG
  2.2 AA). `ui-designer` (self-check), `flow-reviewer` (gate), `/design-review` all load it.
- **`usability-analytics` skill** = the empirical-validation canon (metrics + UX benchmarks +
  triangulation + stats caution). `data-analyst` runs it; `ux-designer` validates against its verdicts.
  Expert review + empirical data are complementary, not redundant.
- **`rebind` skill** = the consume-verification procedure. `consumer-migrator` runs it across files.

**Quality gate (the delivery seam)** — `ui-designer` builds incrementally, render-verifying each
phase, then runs **two Figma gates at delivery**: the **design-review self-check** (its build-time
application of the `ux-flow-review` canon — zero blockers) AND the **Gotcha #27 binding audit** on any
new frame built outside {{SYSTEM_NAME}} instances — zero unbound. Then **`flow-reviewer` runs the same canon
independently** as the usability gate (a fresh evaluator catches what the builder rationalized away).
A screen is not done until all pass.

**Usability-validation gate (required, before handoff).** The Figma gates verify *fidelity +
compliance*; they do not prove the design *works for users*. So every flow bound for product +
engineering is first **usability-tested as a coded prototype** (`usability-prototype`) — cohort
separation, Clarity heatmaps, PostHog time-on-task, post-task SEQ. Task success / time-on-task / SEQ
must clear before handoff; a failure routes back to `ux-designer` / `ui-designer`, not forward. This
is a gate, not an optional extra — designs do not go live or reach engineers unvalidated.

