## The pipeline (this context's slice)

```yaml
screen_creation_pipeline:
  1_ux:      define flows + state matrix + acceptance criteria + functional copy (ux-designer)
  2_gap?:    new pattern/component needed? → file a request to the DS context; wait or stub
  3_ui:      compose {{SYSTEM_NAME}} into the screen; build incrementally, render-verify each phase (ui-designer)
  4_ui:      Figma gates — design-review self-check (zero blockers, ux-flow-review canon) + Gotcha #27 (zero unbound)
  4b_review: INDEPENDENT heuristic evaluation — flow-reviewer runs the ux-flow-review canon as the gate
  5_proto:   build + instrument the coded prototype; run the usability test (usability-prototype)
  6_analyze: data-analyst benchmarks the behavior (usability-analytics) → validation evidence
  6b_validate: usability GATE — ux-designer validates screens vs the evidence (success/time/SEQ/drop-off); pass → handoff
  7_handoff: hand the VALIDATED screens to the product team + engineers → go live
  feedback:
    ui_to_ds:   "{{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap found while building" → ds-steward + component-designer build + publish it
    ux_to_ds:   "new interaction pattern needs a component" → DS context, before ui-designer builds
    review_back: flow-reviewer finds a blocker → back to ux-designer/ui-designer, never forward
    data_back:  data-analyst invalidates a screen → back to ux-designer/ui-designer; inconclusive → re-test
    proto_to_ux: usability test surfaces a problem → back to ux-designer/ui-designer before handoff
    ds_to_here: "{{SYSTEM_NAME}} republished" → refresh the read-only skill mirrors, THEN run consumer-migrator
                (rebind) to swap stale instances onto the fresh main + verify it's actually consumed
```

> **Consume-verification loop (the point of `rebind` + `consumer-migrator`):** a DS publish is
> not "used" until consumer instances are swapped onto the fresh main — they cache old layout until
> then (Gotcha #20). After any publish that affects screens in scope, run `/rebind` (or the skill
> interactively) so we KNOW the change propagated; the per-file table with `0 unbound` + verified is
> the proof. A bad freshly-published main is a DS gap, not a rebind — route it back.

## Heuristic canon (DESIGN.md §6, applied at the SCREEN + FLOW layer)

The DS context applies the §6 frameworks at the system/component layer; **this** context owns the
screen- and flow-level slices that the DS context explicitly defers:

| Pipeline step | §6 heuristics that govern it | Applied as a concrete check |
|---|---|---|
| **1 · define UX** (`ux-designer`) | Shneiderman (closure · locus of control) · Tognazzini (anticipation · autonomy · explorability) · Gerhardt-Powals (automate workload) | Complete state matrix (default/loading/empty/error/success); user keeps control (back/cancel/undo, flow exits); minimize recall + cognitive load per step. |
| **2 · gap routing** | Weinschenk (System Capabilities) | A missing pattern is a DS request, not a hand-built one-off — the published library is the meaningful aid. |
| **3 · build** (`ui-designer`) | Gestalt (proximity/similarity/common-region/figure-ground) · hierarchy (one primary action) · Laws of UX (Fitts · Hick · Miller · Jakob) · Weinschenk (**Navigation**) | Compose {{SYSTEM_NAME}}; one primary CTA per screen in the thumb-reach zone on {{FRAME_W}}×{{FRAME_H}}; familiar {{DOMAIN}} patterns; chunk fields. |
| **4 · review gate** (`ui-designer`) | Nielsen 10 (error PREVENTION weighted for {{DOMAIN}} · user control · consistency · plain-language recovery) · Weinschenk (**Error Prevention · User Feedback**) · WCAG 2.2 AA | Block bad input before submit; irreversible actions gated by Dialog confirmation; AA contrast + 44×44 targets + visible focus + logical order. |
| **5 · prototype + usability test** | Tognazzini (efficiency · visible navigation) · Gerhardt-Powals (meaningful aids) | REQUIRED before handoff: instrument task success + time-on-task + SEQ; cohort separation; heatmaps; reduced-motion respected. |
| **6 · analyze + validate** (`data-analyst` → `ux-designer`) | Gerhardt-Powals (reduce uncertainty · fuse data) · Tognazzini (efficiency) · Weinschenk (User Feedback) | Benchmark behavior vs UX norms (success ≈78%+, SEQ ≥5.5, time vs target, drop-off); triangulate quant + Clarity; validate / invalidate / re-test with stated confidence. Failure routes back, not forward. |
| **7 · handoff** | Weinschenk (System Capabilities · User Feedback) | Only *data-validated* screens reach product + engineering / go live. |
| _DS context — NOT applied here_ | Rams · Shneiderman (consistency/memory) · Gerhardt-Powals (data-fusion) at the **token/component** layer | Token + component construction — applied where {{SYSTEM_NAME}} is authored, not where screens are built. |

## Boundary calls

```yaml
compose_vs_build:  ui-designer COMPOSES {{SYSTEM_NAME}} instances · never hand-builds a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} equivalent.
                   A row / amount field / inner-screen header / dialog → use the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} component
                   (List Item / Input Amount / Top Nav State=Screen / Dialog) or file a gap.
specs_vs_pixels:   ux-designer writes SPECS (no Figma pixels) · ui-designer places pixels ·
                   neither touches token/component internals (that's the DS context).
microcopy:         ux-designer owns FUNCTIONAL product copy (labels/errors/empty), named with
                   spiel-friendly keys (`<screen>/<element>`) so the DS context can tokenize them.
                   brand-designer (DS context) owns expressive/marketing voice. One shared glossary.
gaps:              any "{{SYSTEM_NAME}} is missing X" → request to the DS context; this context waits or stubs,
                   never mutates the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} source.
```

