## Operating rules for the desktop session

**1. Plan Mode before any consumer-file write.** A screen build mutates the shared consumer file
(`{{CONSUMER_FIGMA_KEY}}`). Plan in `yaml`, list component instances (keys) + expected bindings +
honest gaps, and approve before building.

**2. MCP minimalism — a SESSION-level setting.** For screen work connect only **Figma + GitHub**
(+ **Notion** if briefs live there); disconnect the rest. Idle connectors burn context-window tokens
and widen the prompt-injection surface.

**3. Load fresh, never from memory.** Agents read `skills/*.md` / `DESIGN.md` at runtime. The mirrors
(`ds-tokens`, `ds-components`, `figma-gotchas`) are read-only snapshots — refresh them after
a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish rather than trusting stale memory.

**4. Compose, don't reinvent.** Hand-building a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} equivalent is the boundary violation that creates
drift. Use the component or file a gap.

**5. Two delivery gates.** Design-review lens (zero blockers) + Gotcha #27 binding audit (zero
unbound on new frames) before a screen is "done."

**6. Prototypes carry no secrets in git.** `.env` + `.vercel` stay gitignored.

