## Separate context — the design system

By design, this context is **screen + prototype only**. The {{SYSTEM_NAME}} design system — tokens, styles,
components, variants, bindings, the manifest, publish, drift, the spiels mechanism — lives in the
separate **`{{DS_REPO}}`** repo, with the `ds-steward` (steward/auditor/publisher),
`component-designer` (builder), and `brand-designer` (identity) agents.

**Handoff across the boundary:** the DS context publishes {{SYSTEM_NAME}} + updates its `skills/`+`manifest/`;
**this** context consumes the published library to build. A {{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap found while building a screen
comes back as a tokenization/component request — the DS context builds + publishes it; this context
waits or stubs. `DESIGN.md` is shared ground truth both read.

---

## Relationship to the bootstrap

`CLAUDE.md` / `CONTEXT.md` boot the session with project facts, file keys, version, and preferences.
`DESIGN.md` is the design-principles source the agents read. The two agents (`ux-designer`,
`ui-designer`) are the execution specialists this context delegates to after boot. The canonical
workflows live **inside the agents** (Claude Code); `kickoff-prompts/*.md` are reference recipes the
agents and you can pull from.

> Note on surface: consumer Figma *writes* run through `use_figma` + the Desktop Bridge. Coded
> prototypes are ordinary local dev (Vite) — in-scope here (unlike the DS context, which never emits code).
